{"id":7176,"date":"2022-08-06T11:13:15","date_gmt":"2022-08-06T11:13:15","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?post_type=student&#038;p=7176"},"modified":"2022-08-06T14:30:42","modified_gmt":"2022-08-06T14:30:42","slug":"rachael-k-kyalo-kenya","status":"publish","type":"student","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/student\/rachael-k-kyalo-kenya\/","title":{"rendered":"Rachael K. Kyalo"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover has-background-dim profile-banner bg-alt\" style=\"background-color:none\"><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n\n\n<a href=\"javascript:history.back()\"> <div class=\"profiles-btn\"> \n\n<div class=\"btn-left-sq bg-primary\"> <i class=\"fa fa-caret-left white-text\"> <\/i> <\/div>\n<div class=\"btn-text title-bold white-text\">Back to Profiles<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/a>\n\n<h2 class=\"profile-name\">Rachael K. Kyalo<\/h2>\n\n<p class=\"primary-bold profile-position prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>Kenya<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-info profile-tagline primary-bold prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>PhD Student &#8211; The Otto Friedrich University of Bamberg, Germany<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5 profile-body\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2022\/08\/Rachael.jpg\"\/>\n\n<p class=\"profile-testimonial invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-success invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n<p class=\"profile-studentbio invis\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span> <\/p>\n\n\n<p>Racheal K. Kyalo is a PhD student at The Otto Friedrich University of Bamberg \u2013 Germany. Her research in Statistics focusing on <em>Small Area Estimation<\/em> is the road to ascertaining that nobody is left out. In pursuit of the same, the Global Indicator Framework of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) advocates disaggregating data in small areas\/domains, for instance, according to gender, income, Geographic location, disability, etc. In simple terms, her research focuses on using Small Area Estimation to help solve the SDGs. Racheal\u2019s research focuses on SDGs 1, 2, 3, 5 and 13 &#8211; Poverty, zero hunger, good health and wellbeing, Gender equality, and climate action.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>In her own words, \u201cher life began at AIMS, AIMS Ghana formed her\u201d. It was at AIMS that her life found direction and focus. At AIMS, she learned that understanding concepts is much better than just excellent grades. As a DAAD PhD scholar, Racheal learnt about DAAD at AIMS Ghana through a seminar.<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Racheal K. Kyalo is a PhD student at The Otto Friedrich University of Bamberg \u2013 Germany. Her research in Statistics focusing on Small Area Estimation is the road to ascertaining that nobody is left out. In pursuit of the same, the Global Indicator Framework of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) advocates disaggregating data in small<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":12,"featured_media":7177,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":"","profile-testimonial":"","profile-success":"","profile-studentbio":"","profile-studentname":"Rachael K. Kyalo","profile-country":"Kenya","profile-program":"PhD Student - The Otto Friedrich University of Bamberg, Germany"},"tags":[],"student_types":[13],"acf":[],"featured_img":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2022\/08\/Rachael.jpg","coauthors":[],"author_meta":{"author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/joel\/","display_name":"joel"},"relative_dates":{"created":"Posted 3 years ago","modified":"Updated 3 years ago"},"absolute_dates":{"created":"Posted on August 6, 2022","modified":"Updated on August 6, 2022"},"absolute_dates_time":{"created":"Posted on August 6